        <item>
            <title>0.12.4</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:47:42 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.12.4</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.12.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.12.4</h2>
<ul>
<li>Pill library: the search list shows one card per pill — the pill&#x27;s face, its name, what it does (e.g. &quot;Shortcut · ⌘K&quot;, &quot;App · Notion&quot;, &quot;Link · notion.so&quot;), and where it lives (&quot;Play · slot 3&quot;, &quot;DaVinci Resolve · Context menu · slot 6&quot;, &quot;Not on any menu&quot;); each pill appears once (no duplicates across History / Saved / Menus)</li>
<li>Pill library: pull down on the categories to reveal the search list — a short pull springs back, a deliberate pull commits; Cancel fades back to the categories; the library is a full-height column at the screen edge with Apple-glass category cards</li>
<li>Arrange mode: switch between your menus without leaving arrange — four menu buttons on the bar (left of undo) wearing the Compass pills&#x27; faces; the hub no longer shows an ✕ in arrange mode</li>
<li>New pill type: System → **Arrange Mode** — a pill that puts the open menu into arrange mode (obeys the click-only / hard-press safeguards like any pill)</li>
<li>Settings: the menu-bar &quot;Settings…&quot; now opens a compact side panel with the everyday settings (Menu · Blur · Sounds · General); &quot;All Settings…&quot; opens the full window</li>
<li>Compass: a lane that isn&#x27;t available right now dims only its glyph — the pill body stays; a switch that is refused in the opening beat does nothing instead of opening the launcher as a folder</li>
<li>Fixed: the goo strand could stay attached after resting on a pill and moving back to the centre</li>
<li>Fixed: the pill library vanished behind the blur when a screenshot shortcut (e.g. Shottr&#x27;s ⇧⌘2) was pressed during arrange</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
